# AI Code Generation Guardrails

> Testing guideline

## Testing Mindset

### Test basics
- When asserting use test input params/models as the source, not constants
- Prefer assertions of input and output models rather than param to target model

### Test What Matters
- Critical paths: auth, validations, data mutation
- Edge cases and error conditions
- Integration points

### Test Must Have
- Test name convention {methodName}_{WhatCaseWeAreChecking}_{ExpectedResult}. {WhatCaseWeAreChecking and {ExpectedResult}
should be capitalized
- Use random values when possible from ThreadLocalRandom/EnhancedRandom/Instancio/other randomization tool that is used
in the project
- Comparison of BigDecimals should be done with `BigDecimal.compareTo(BigDecimal)`. You need to find
`assertBigDecimalEquals` in the code base or use the following code snippet

```java
public static void assertBigDecimalEquals(@Nullable BigDecimal first, @Nullable BigDecimal second) {
    final String errorMessage = "BigDecimals are not equal. Expected %s. Actual %s".formatted(first, second);
    if ((first == null) != (second == null)) {
        throw buildFailure(first, second, errorMessage);
    }
    if (first == null) {
        return;
    }

    Assertions.assertEquals(0, first.compareTo(second), errorMessage);
}

private static AssertionFailedError buildFailure(
        @Nullable BigDecimal first, @Nullable BigDecimal second, String errorMessage) {
    return assertionFailure()
            .message(errorMessage)
            .expected(first)
            .actual(second)
            .build();
}
```

### Integration tests
- All tests MUST be isolated and independent
- Each test should not depend on the state from other tests
- Use `@BeforeEach` to reset mocks and clear state like recreate topic or cleanup DB table
- If there is audit then verify that they're in place. for example, createdAt and updatedAt are present after creation.
CreatedAt stayed the same but updatedAt was changed after update. To check that updatedAt was changed correctly use
```java
org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat(savedBonusTemplateAuditEntity.getModifiedAt())
                .isCloseTo(savedBonusTemplateEntity.getModifiedAt(), within(1, ChronoUnit.MILLIS));
```
- No mocking services, repositories, etc. Use real beans and testcontainers. Mocking is allowed only for external HTTP
calls
- For assertions you must use org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions

### Parameterized Tests
- Tests SHOULD be written parameterized when possible
- Use `@ParameterizedTest` with `@MethodSource` for complex scenarios. Write descriptive name as first parameter and put
 it in name like @ParameterizedTest(name = "{0}")
- If there multiple parametrized tests which are using the same method source then reuse this method source. If those
tests are in different classes then move data for method source to abstract parent class

### Required Containers
 - **PostgreSQLContainer** - Database testing
 - **RedisContainer** - Cache testing (if needed)
 - **KafkaContainer** - Message broker testing
 - **MockServerContainer** - External API mocking

### Container Management
 - Containers are started once and reused (singleton pattern)
 - Use `@DynamicPropertySource` to override Spring properties